---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ContactUs from "../../components/astro/ContactUs.astro";
import LogoHoneycomb from "../../components/astro/LogoHoneycomb.astro";
import "../../styles/contract-workflow.css";
const title = "HubSpot Contract Management Setup";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description="Reduce manual customer-contract work in HubSpot. Discuss PandaDoc setup, selected field updates and signed-document handoffs. Free initial workflow call.">
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<header class="header wrap">
  <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="SwotBee home"><LogoHoneycomb width={32} height={30} /><span>SWOT<span class="brand-bee">bee</span></span></a>
  <nav aria-label="Page navigation"><a href="#scope">How we help</a><a href="#process">The process</a><a href="#questions">Questions</a></nav>
  <a class="button button-small" href="#inquiry" data-ga-cta="contract_workflow_request">Discuss your workflow <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
</header>
<main id="main">
  <div class="hero-surface"><section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span>PANDADOC + HUBSPOT WORKFLOW SETUP</div>
      <h1 id="hero-title">Get help connecting your <span class="highlight">contracts</span> to HubSpot.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">Still copying details from signed contracts into HubSpot? SwotBee helps you scope and configure a customer-contract workflow, from preparing the document to keeping the right deal record up to date.</p>
      <a class="button" href="#inquiry" data-ga-cta="contract_workflow_request">Request a workflow call <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <p class="cta-note">Free initial conversation. Implementation scoped separately.</p>
      <p class="other-tools">Using DocuSign or another tool? <a href="#inquiry" data-ga-cta="contract_workflow_request">Tell us what you use.</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="workflow-art" role="img" aria-label="Illustrative workflow: prepare a customer agreement from deal data, complete signing, then review selected fields and the signed PDF on the linked HubSpot deal. This is an example, not a product screenshot.">
      <div class="art-topline"><span class="tiny-dot"></span>ONE AGREEMENT. A CLEAR HANDOFF.<span class="example-label">Example</span></div>
      <div class="document-card">
        <div class="document-head"><div class="document-icon" aria-hidden="true">▤</div><span>CUSTOMER AGREEMENT</span><span class="paper-number">01</span></div>
        <h2>Annual support agreement</h2><p class="doc-sub">Example Services · Support deal</p>
        <div class="document-lines"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
        <div class="document-fields"><div><span>Customer reference</span><strong>CLIENT-101</strong></div><div><span>Term end</span><strong>30 Nov 2027</strong></div></div>
        <div class="signature"><span class="signature-script">Example signature</span><span class="status"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span> Signed</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="transfer"><span class="transfer-line"></span><span class="transfer-pill"><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span> Selected details + signed PDF</span><span class="transfer-line"></span></div>
      <div class="deal-card"><div class="deal-top"><div class="crm-icon" aria-hidden="true">H</div><div><span class="deal-kicker">HUBSPOT DEAL</span><h3>Example Services / Support</h3></div><span class="deal-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><div class="deal-bottom"><span><span class="check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span> Linked agreement</span><span class="review-badge">Ready for review</span></div></div>
      <div class="art-foot"><span class="shield" aria-hidden="true">◇</span> Check the record. Verify the handoff.</div>
    </div>
  </section>
  </div>
  <section class="principles wrap" aria-label="Service approach"><div><span class="mini-index">01</span><strong>Your existing tools, reviewed first</strong></div><div><span class="mini-index">02</span><strong>One clearly scoped workflow</strong></div><div><span class="mini-index">03</span><strong>A useful next step, before a project</strong></div></section>
  <section class="pain-section" aria-labelledby="pain-title"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">THE MANUAL WORK BETWEEN THE TOOLS</span><h2 id="pain-title">Which step is slowing<br> your team down?</h2></div><p>Your contract may be signed.<br> The work around it often isn’t finished.</p></div>
    <div class="pain-grid">
      <article><span class="number">01 / PREPARE</span><div class="line-icon" aria-hidden="true">▤<span>↺</span></div><h3>Entering the same<br> details. Again.</h3><p>Re-entering deal details every time you prepare a contract.</p></article>
      <article><span class="number">02 / UPDATE</span><div class="line-icon" aria-hidden="true">⇄</div><h3>Signed there.<br> Copied over here.</h3><p>Copying selected information back into HubSpot after signing.</p></article>
      <article><span class="number">03 / HAND OVER</span><div class="line-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌕</div><h3>Now, where’s<br> the signed copy?</h3><p>Finding the executed agreement and checking which deal it belongs to.</p></article>
    </div>
    <div class="section-afterword">Tell us where the handoff breaks. We’ll look at one workflow with you before proposing changes.<a href="#inquiry" data-ga-cta="contract_workflow_request">Let’s discuss it <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </div></section>
  <section id="scope" class="scope-section wrap" aria-labelledby="scope-title">
    <div class="scope-intro"><span class="eyebrow">WHAT A SCOPED IMPLEMENTATION CAN COVER</span><h2 id="scope-title">Less moving information.<br> More useful handoffs.</h2><p>The right setup starts with your process. We assess your current tools before proposing custom work.</p><div class="scope-note"><span aria-hidden="true">↳</span><p>Existing native configuration may be sufficient. We’ll start there.</p></div></div>
    <div class="scope-list"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Prepare from reviewed deal data</h3><p>Set up an approved template around the fields your team already maintains.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Bring selected document values back</h3><p>Configure supported mappings and completion rules for the agreed fields and signing route.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Make the handoff usable</h3><p>Keep the executed agreement with the intended deal and give the responsible person a verification and recovery checklist.</p></div></article><p class="scope-qualifier">The scope depends on your tools, subscriptions, templates and business rules.</p></div>
  </section>
  <section class="example-section wrap" aria-labelledby="example-title"><div class="example-panel"><div><span class="eyebrow">A WORKED EXAMPLE</span><h2 id="example-title">One customer.<br> Two deals.<br> The right agreement.</h2><p>A support agreement starts from the intended deal. After signing, selected details return to the linked record and the completed PDF is retained there. The operator checks the handoff before the next team acts.</p></div><div class="example-map"><div class="customer-node"><span class="node-icon" aria-hidden="true">E</span><div><small>CUSTOMER</small><strong>Example Services</strong></div></div><div class="map-branch" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="map-deals"><div class="map-deal selected"><span class="map-label">Support deal</span><strong>Annual agreement</strong><span class="map-tag"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span> Linked document</span></div><div class="map-deal"><span class="map-label">Separate project</span><strong>Project agreement</strong><span class="map-muted">Separate record</span></div></div><p>Illustrative workflow, not a customer result.<br> Account setup and acceptance checks are confirmed during implementation.</p></div></div></section>
  <section id="process" class="process-section wrap" aria-labelledby="process-title"><div class="center-heading"><span class="eyebrow">A SMALL FIRST STEP</span><h2 id="process-title">Start with a conversation.<br> Decide on the project after.</h2></div><div class="process-grid"><article><span class="step-circle">1</span><h3>Tell Sharmi about the workflow</h3><p>Explain what you do today, which tools you use and what you want to change.</p></article><article><span class="step-circle">2</span><h3>Get a short recap</h3><p>We identify the likely route, important dependencies and an appropriate next step.</p></article><article><span class="step-circle">3</span><h3>Choose whether to proceed</h3><p>If paid implementation fits, receive a separate scope with deliverables, costs and acceptance checks.</p></article></div><p class="process-footnote">No contract uploads or account credentials needed for the initial conversation.</p></section>
  <section id="questions" class="faq-section wrap" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><div><span class="eyebrow">A FEW THINGS TO KNOW</span><h2 id="faq-title">Before we talk.</h2><p>A clear scope starts with<br> clear expectations.</p></div><div class="faq-list">
    <details open><summary>Is this software or an implementation service?<span aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p>This is an implementation service. We assess your existing workflow and propose the appropriate configuration or integration work.</p></details>
    <details><summary>We already have an integration. Can you still help?<span aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p>Yes. Describe what works and what still requires manual work. We first assess whether your existing configuration can meet the need.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Do we have to change signing tools?<span aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p>A change is not assumed. Tell us your current tools and constraints. The PandaDoc example does not establish identical functionality in another tool.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What does implementation cost?<span aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p>It is quoted after the workflow and dependencies are understood. The quote distinguishes implementation from additional vendor licenses or recurring tool costs.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can we discuss renewals or other contract work?<span aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p>Yes. Describe the job you need help with. Renewal tracking, migration, billing changes or additional templates are assessed and scoped separately.</p></details>
  </div></section>
  <section id="inquiry" class="inquiry-section" aria-labelledby="inquiry-title"><div class="wrap inquiry-grid"><div class="inquiry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">LET’S LOOK AT YOUR WORKFLOW</span><h2 id="inquiry-title">What would you<br> like to stop<br> <span>doing manually?</span></h2><p>Tell us about your customer-contract workflow. We’ll assess whether a workflow call is a useful next step.</p><div class="person"><div class="person-avatar" aria-hidden="true">S</div><div><strong>You’ll speak with Sharmi</strong><span>Discovery, scoping and implementation</span></div></div><div class="offer-note"><strong>Free initial conversation + short recap</strong><p>Implementation is optional, separately scoped and quoted.</p></div></div>
    <div class="form-card inquiry-form"><h3>Request a workflow call</h3><p class="form-intro">A sentence about your current process is enough.</p><ContactUs variant="contract-workflow" preview={false} /><p class="form-intro">Prefer email? <a href="mailto:info@swotbee.com">Contact info@swotbee.com</a>.</p></div>
  </div></section>
</main>
<footer class="footer wrap"><a class="brand" href="#main" aria-label="SwotBee, back to top"><LogoHoneycomb width={32} height={30} /><span>SWOT<span class="brand-bee">bee</span></span></a><p>Independent implementation services.<br> HubSpot and PandaDoc are third-party platforms.</p><span class="footer-review"><a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> · <a href="/terms/">Terms</a> · <a href="/contactus/">Contact</a><br /><button type="button" data-consent-reopen>Cookie settings</button></span></footer>

</BaseLayout>
